{"name":"Sandal","hex":"#a3876a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sandal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A suburb of Wakefield, West Yorkshire, England ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sandal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sandal","blocks":[{"text":"Sandals are an open type of footwear consisting of a sole held to the wearer's foot by straps that go over the instep and around the ankle. Sandals may also feature a heel of varying heights. While the distinction between sandals and other types of footwear can sometimes be unclear, sandals are generally understood to leave most of the foot exposed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Men%27s_size_10_Sandals.jpg/330px-Men%27s_size_10_Sandals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg/500px-Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg/1280px-Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg/500px-Sandalias_de_esparto_%2829139609730%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Esparto sandals from the 6th or 5th millennium BC found in Spain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASandalias_de_esparto_(29139609730).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Egyptian_sandals%2C_vegetable_fiber_-_Bata_Shoe_Museum_-_DSC00009.JPG/500px-Egyptian_sandals%2C_vegetable_fiber_-_Bata_Shoe_Museum_-_DSC00009.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.